role based access control (RBAC) in Spring Security allows you to restrict access to
certain parts of your application based on the roles assigned to users.
You can define roles such as "ROLE_USER", "ROLE_ADMIN", etc.,
and then use annotations like @PreAuthorize or @Secured to specify which roles are
required to access specific methods or endpoints.
For example, you can use @PreAuthorize("hasRole('ROLE_ADMIN')") to restrict access to
a method